IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2017, VALUE OF ALLOTMENT (7 U.S.C. 2017), lines 1261-1339 of usc07-ch51.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's side. Amounts the Act leaves to the Secretary (the cost of the thrifty
-- food plan, the standardized procedures of subsection (f)) are INPUTS; the fiscal year 2027 figures are in snap3-s2017-cola.l4.
-- A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say.
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars. Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

-- TYPES. Every type and constructor begins with the label of the provision that needs it.
DECLARE `s 2017(c)(1) initial allotment` IS ONE OF
    `s 2017(c)(1) no allotment may be issued`
    `s 2017(c)(1) an allotment of`
        HAS `s 2017(c)(1) the value of the initial allotment` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2017(c)(1) not covered`

DECLARE `s 2017(c)(3) provisions that govern the combined allotment` IS ONE OF
    `s 2017(c)(3) section 2020(e)(3) governs`
    `s 2017(c)(3) paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) govern`

§ `s 2017 -- value of allotment`

§§ `s 2017(a) calculation`

-- src:1262 | (a) Calculation
-- src:1263 | The value of the allotment which State agencies shall be authorized to issue to any households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be equal to the cost to such households of the thrifty food plan reduced by an amount equal to 30 per centum of the household’s income, as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e) of this title, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar: Provided, That for households of one and two persons the minimum allotment shall be 8 percent of the cost of the thrifty food plan for a household containing 1 member, as determined by the Secretary under section 2012 of this title, rounded to the nearest whole dollar increment.
@ref s 2017(a) calculation (src:1262-1263)
-- In plain words: the allotment is the cost of the thrifty food plan for the household, less 30 per cent of the household's income as worked out under
-- section 2014(d) and (e), rounded down to a whole dollar. The cost and the income arrive as inputs.
GIVEN `the cost to the household of the thrifty food plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the household's income as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2017(a) the cost of the thrifty food plan reduced by 30 per centum of income, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the cost to the household of the thrifty food plan` MINUS 0.30 TIMES `the household's income as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e)`)

-- src:1262 | (a) Calculation
-- src:1263 | The value of the allotment which State agencies shall be authorized to issue to any households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be equal to the cost to such households of the thrifty food plan reduced by an amount equal to 30 per centum of the household’s income, as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e) of this title, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar: Provided, That for households of one and two persons the minimum allotment shall be 8 percent of the cost of the thrifty food plan for a household containing 1 member, as determined by the Secretary under section 2012 of this title, rounded to the nearest whole dollar increment.
@ref s 2017(a) proviso, the minimum allotment for households of one and two persons (src:1262-1263)
-- In plain words: 8 per cent of the plan's cost for a one-member household, rounded to the nearest whole dollar. The text does not say which way a half goes:
-- half up is taken here (assumed, not ruled; see NOTES.md fork F-2017-1).
GIVEN `the cost of the thrifty food plan for a household containing 1 member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2017(a) the minimum allotment, 8 percent of the cost for 1 member rounded to the nearest whole dollar` MEANS
    FLOOR (0.08 TIMES `the cost of the thrifty food plan for a household containing 1 member` PLUS 0.5)

-- src:1262 | (a) Calculation
-- src:1263 | The value of the allotment which State agencies shall be authorized to issue to any households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be equal to the cost to such households of the thrifty food plan reduced by an amount equal to 30 per centum of the household’s income, as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e) of this title, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar: Provided, That for households of one and two persons the minimum allotment shall be 8 percent of the cost of the thrifty food plan for a household containing 1 member, as determined by the Secretary under section 2012 of this title, rounded to the nearest whole dollar increment.
@ref s 2017(a) the value of the allotment the State agency is authorized to issue (src:1262-1263)
-- In plain words: for a certified household the allotment is the reduced cost; a household of one or two persons gets at least the minimum allotment.
-- A household of three or more whose reduced cost is below zero has no figure in the text.
GIVEN `the household has been certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons in the household` IS A NUMBER
      `the cost to the household of the thrifty food plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the household's income as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum allotment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2017(a) the value of the allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the household has been certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            NOTHING
        IF `the number of persons in the household` LESS THAN 1 THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
            NOTHING
        IF `the number of persons in the household` AT MOST 2 THEN
            JUST (max (`s 2017(a) the cost of the thrifty food plan reduced by 30 per centum of income, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar` `the cost to the household of the thrifty food plan` `the household's income as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e)`) `the minimum allotment`)
        IF `s 2017(a) the cost of the thrifty food plan reduced by 30 per centum of income, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar` `the cost to the household of the thrifty food plan` `the household's income as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e)` AT LEAST 0 THEN
            JUST (`s 2017(a) the cost of the thrifty food plan reduced by 30 per centum of income, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar` `the cost to the household of the thrifty food plan` `the household's income as determined in accordance with section 2014(d) and (e)`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives no value when the reduced cost is below zero for a household of three or more
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2017(b) benefits not deemed income or resources for certain purposes`

-- src:1264 | (b) Benefits not deemed income or resources for certain purposes
-- src:1265 | The value of benefits that may be provided under this chapter shall not be considered income or resources for any purpose under any Federal, State, or local laws, including, but not limited to, laws relating to taxation, welfare, and public assistance programs, and no participating State or political subdivision thereof shall decrease any assistance otherwise provided an individual or individuals because of the receipt of benefits under this chapter.
@ref s 2017(b) the value of benefits is not income or resources for any purpose under Federal, State or local law (src:1264-1265)
-- In plain words: for any purpose under a Federal, State or local law (taxation, welfare, public assistance and the rest), the value of SNAP benefits is neither income nor resources.
GIVEN `the purpose is one under a Federal, State or local law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(b) the value of the benefits is considered income or resources for the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the purpose is one under a Federal, State or local law` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be considered income or resources for any purpose under any Federal, State, or local laws"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any purpose under any Federal, State, or local laws"
            NOTHING

-- src:1264 | (b) Benefits not deemed income or resources for certain purposes
-- src:1265 | The value of benefits that may be provided under this chapter shall not be considered income or resources for any purpose under any Federal, State, or local laws, including, but not limited to, laws relating to taxation, welfare, and public assistance programs, and no participating State or political subdivision thereof shall decrease any assistance otherwise provided an individual or individuals because of the receipt of benefits under this chapter.
@ref s 2017(b) no participating State or political subdivision shall decrease other assistance because of the receipt of benefits (src:1264-1265)
-- In plain words: a State or local government that takes part in the program may not cut the assistance it otherwise gives a person because that person receives SNAP benefits.
GIVEN `the body is a participating State or political subdivision of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is otherwise provided to the individual or individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decrease is because of the receipt of benefits under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(b) the participating State or political subdivision may decrease the assistance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body is a participating State or political subdivision of one` AND `the assistance is otherwise provided to the individual or individuals` AND `the decrease is because of the receipt of benefits under this chapter` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no participating State or political subdivision thereof shall decrease any assistance otherwise provided an individual or individuals because of the receipt of benefits under this chapter"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "because of the receipt of benefits under this chapter"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2017(c) first month benefits prorated`

-- src:1266 | (c) First month benefits prorated
-- src:1267 | (1) The value of the allotment issued to any eligible household for the initial month or other initial period for which an allotment is issued shall have a value which bears the same ratio to the value of the allotment for a full month or other initial period for which the allotment is issued as the number of days (from the date of application) remaining in the month or other initial period for which the allotment is issued bears to the total number of days in the month or other initial period for which the allotment is issued, except that no allotment may be issued to a household for the initial month or period if the value of the allotment which such household would otherwise be eligible to receive under this subsection is less than $10. Households shall receive full months’ allotments for all months within a certification period, except as provided in the first sentence of this paragraph with respect to an initial month.
@ref s 2017(c)(1) the value of the allotment for an initial month or period (src:1266-1267)
-- In plain words: the first allotment is the full allotment times (days left from the application date) divided by (days in the month or period), but nothing is issued if that comes to less than $10.
-- The text does not round the result, and does not say whether the application day itself counts as a day remaining: the application day is counted here (NOTES.md fork F-2017-2).
GIVEN `the value of the allotment for a full month or other initial period` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of application` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the month or other initial period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the month or other initial period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 2017(c)(1) initial allotment`
`s 2017(c)(1) the initial allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the total number of days` LESS THAN 1 OR `the number of days remaining` LESS THAN 1 OR `the number of days remaining` GREATER THAN `the total number of days` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the application date is not inside the month or period
            `s 2017(c)(1) not covered`
        IF `the proportion of the full allotment` LESS THAN 10 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no allotment may be issued to a household for the initial month or period if the value of the allotment which such household would otherwise be eligible to receive under this subsection is less than $10"
            `s 2017(c)(1) no allotment may be issued`
        OTHERWISE
            `s 2017(c)(1) an allotment of` `the proportion of the full allotment`
    WHERE
        `the number of days remaining` MEANS Day `the last day of the month or other initial period` MINUS Day `the date of application` PLUS 1
        `the total number of days` MEANS Day `the last day of the month or other initial period` MINUS Day `the first day of the month or other initial period` PLUS 1
        `the proportion of the full allotment` MEANS `the value of the allotment for a full month or other initial period` TIMES `the number of days remaining` DIVIDED BY `the total number of days`

-- src:1267 | (1) The value of the allotment issued to any eligible household for the initial month or other initial period for which an allotment is issued shall have a value which bears the same ratio to the value of the allotment for a full month or other initial period for which the allotment is issued as the number of days (from the date of application) remaining in the month or other initial period for which the allotment is issued bears to the total number of days in the month or other initial period for which the allotment is issued, except that no allotment may be issued to a household for the initial month or period if the value of the allotment which such household would otherwise be eligible to receive under this subsection is less than $10. Households shall receive full months’ allotments for all months within a certification period, except as provided in the first sentence of this paragraph with respect to an initial month.
@ref s 2017(c)(1) full months' allotments within a certification period (src:1267)
-- In plain words: every month inside a certification period gets a full allotment, except an initial month.
GIVEN `the month is within a certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is an initial month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(c)(1) the household receives the full month's allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the month is within a certification period` AND `the month is an initial month` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except as provided in the first sentence of this paragraph with respect to an initial month"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the month is within a certification period` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for all months within a certification period"
            NOTHING

-- src:1268 | (2) As used in this subsection, the term “initial month” means (A) the first month for which an allotment is issued to a household, (B) the first month for which an allotment is issued to a household following any period in which such household was not participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this chapter after the expiration of a certification period or after the termination of the certification of a household, during a certification period, when the household ceased to be eligible after notice and an opportunity for a hearing under section 2020(e)(10) of this title, and (C) in the case of a migrant or seasonal farmworker household, the first month for which allotment is issued to a household that applies following any period of more than 30 days in which such household was not participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program after previous participation in such program.
@ref s 2017(c)(2) the month is an initial month (src:1268)
-- In plain words: an initial month is (A) the first month ever allotted, (B) the first month after a break that followed the end of a certification period, or the end of one cut short because the
-- household stopped being eligible after notice and a hearing opportunity, or (C) for a migrant or seasonal farmworker household, the first month after a break of more than 30 days.
GIVEN `the month is the first month for which an allotment is issued to the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is the first month for which an allotment is issued following a period of not participating after the expiration of a certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is the first month for which an allotment is issued following a period of not participating after the termination of the certification of the household during a certification period, when the household ceased to be eligible after notice and an opportunity for a hearing under section 2020(e)(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is a migrant or seasonal farmworker household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household applies following a period of not participating, after previous participation, of this many days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(c)(2) the month is an initial month` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the month is the first month for which an allotment is issued to the household` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the month is the first month for which an allotment is issued following a period of not participating after the expiration of a certification period` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the month is the first month for which an allotment is issued following a period of not participating after the termination of the certification of the household during a certification period, when the household ceased to be eligible after notice and an opportunity for a hearing under section 2020(e)(10)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the household is a migrant or seasonal farmworker household` AND `the household applies following a period of not participating, after previous participation, of this many days` GREATER THAN 30 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term “initial month” means"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1269 | (3) Optional combined allotment for expedited households.—
-- src:1270 | A State agency may provide to an eligible household applying after the 15th day of a month, in lieu of the initial allotment of the household and the regular allotment of the household for the following month, an allotment that is equal to the total amount of the initial allotment and the first regular allotment. The allotment shall be provided in accordance with section 2020(e)(3) of this title in the case of a household that is not entitled to expedited service and in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title in the case of a household that is entitled to expedited service.
@ref s 2017(c)(3) optional combined allotment for expedited households (src:1269-1270)
-- In plain words: a State agency may give a household that applies after the 15th of a month one combined allotment instead of the initial one and the next month's.
GIVEN `the household is an eligible household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(c)(3) the State agency may provide a combined allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is an eligible household` AND DATE_DAY `the date of application` GREATER THAN 15 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an eligible household applying after the 15th day of a month"
            NOTHING

-- src:1269 | (3) Optional combined allotment for expedited households.—
-- src:1270 | A State agency may provide to an eligible household applying after the 15th day of a month, in lieu of the initial allotment of the household and the regular allotment of the household for the following month, an allotment that is equal to the total amount of the initial allotment and the first regular allotment. The allotment shall be provided in accordance with section 2020(e)(3) of this title in the case of a household that is not entitled to expedited service and in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title in the case of a household that is entitled to expedited service.
@ref s 2017(c)(3) the combined allotment equals the initial allotment plus the first regular allotment (src:1269-1270)
GIVEN `the initial allotment of the household` IS A NUMBER
      `the first regular allotment of the household for the following month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2017(c)(3) the combined allotment` MEANS
    `the initial allotment of the household` PLUS `the first regular allotment of the household for the following month`

-- src:1269 | (3) Optional combined allotment for expedited households.—
-- src:1270 | A State agency may provide to an eligible household applying after the 15th day of a month, in lieu of the initial allotment of the household and the regular allotment of the household for the following month, an allotment that is equal to the total amount of the initial allotment and the first regular allotment. The allotment shall be provided in accordance with section 2020(e)(3) of this title in the case of a household that is not entitled to expedited service and in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title in the case of a household that is entitled to expedited service.
@ref s 2017(c)(3) which provisions of section 2020(e) the combined allotment is provided under (src:1269-1270)
-- In plain words: under section 2020(e)(3) if the household is not entitled to expedited service; under paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) if it is.
GIVEN `the household is entitled to expedited service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2017(c)(3) provisions that govern the combined allotment`
`s 2017(c)(3) the provisions of section 2020(e) that govern the combined allotment` MEANS
    IF `the household is entitled to expedited service`
    THEN `s 2017(c)(3) paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) govern`
    ELSE `s 2017(c)(3) section 2020(e)(3) governs`

§§ `s 2017(d) reduction of public assistance benefits`

-- src:1271 | (d) Reduction of public assistance benefits
-- src:1272 | (1) In general
-- src:1273 | If the benefits of a household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program, for the duration of the reduction—
-- src:1274 | (A) the household may not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the household to the extent that the decrease is the result of the reduction; and
-- src:1275 | (B) the State agency may reduce the allotment of the household by not more than 25 percent.
@ref s 2017(d)(1) reduction of benefits under a means-tested public assistance program (src:1271-1275)
-- In plain words: while a household's public assistance (a means-tested Federal, State or local program) is cut because a member failed to do what the program requires,
-- (A) a drop in the household's income that results from the cut cannot raise its SNAP allotment, and (B) the State agency may cut the SNAP allotment by up to 25 percent.
GIVEN `the benefits of the household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decrease in the income of the household is the result of the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(d)(1)(A) the household may receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefits of the household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program` AND `the decrease in the income of the household is the result of the reduction` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the household may not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the household to the extent that the decrease is the result of the reduction"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the benefits of a household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program"
            NOTHING

-- src:1271 | (d) Reduction of public assistance benefits
-- src:1272 | (1) In general
-- src:1273 | If the benefits of a household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program, for the duration of the reduction—
-- src:1274 | (A) the household may not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the household to the extent that the decrease is the result of the reduction; and
-- src:1275 | (B) the State agency may reduce the allotment of the household by not more than 25 percent.
@ref s 2017(d)(1)(B) the State agency may reduce the allotment by not more than 25 percent (src:1271-1275)
GIVEN `the benefits of the household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction proposed, as a percentage of the allotment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(d)(1)(B) the State agency may reduce the allotment of the household by the percentage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefits of the household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program` AND `the reduction proposed, as a percentage of the allotment` AT MOST 25 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the State agency may reduce the allotment of the household by not more than 25 percent"
            NOTHING

-- src:1271 | (d) Reduction of public assistance benefits
-- src:1272 | (1) In general
-- src:1273 | If the benefits of a household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program, for the duration of the reduction—
-- src:1274 | (A) the household may not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the household to the extent that the decrease is the result of the reduction; and
-- src:1275 | (B) the State agency may reduce the allotment of the household by not more than 25 percent.
@ref s 2017(d)(1)(B) the most the State agency may take off the allotment (src:1271-1275)
GIVEN `the benefits of the household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment of the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2017(d)(1)(B) the greatest reduction of the allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefits of the household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program for the failure of a member of the household to perform an action required under the law or program` THEN JUST (0.25 TIMES `the allotment of the household`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the benefits of a household are reduced under a Federal, State, or local law"
            NOTHING

-- src:1276 | (2) Rules and procedures
-- src:1277 | If the allotment of a household is reduced under this subsection for a failure to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), the State agency may use the rules and procedures that apply under part A of title IV of the Act to reduce the allotment under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2017(d)(2) rules and procedures of part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (src:1276-1277)
GIVEN `the allotment of the household is reduced under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(d)(2) the State agency may use the rules and procedures that apply under part A of title IV` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the allotment of the household is reduced under this subsection` AND `the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a failure to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2017(e) allotments for households residing in centers`

-- src:1278 | (e) Allotments for households residing in centers
-- src:1279 | (1) In general
-- src:1280 | In the case of an individual who resides in a center for the purpose of a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5) of this title, a State agency may provide an allotment for the individual to—
-- src:1281 | (A) the center as an authorized representative of the individual for a period that is less than 1 month; and
-- src:1282 | (B) the individual, if the individual leaves the center.
@ref s 2017(e)(1)(A) the State agency may provide the allotment to the center as the individual's authorized representative (src:1278-1282)
-- In plain words: for a person living in a center for a drug or alcoholic treatment program (the programs described in section 2012(m)(5)), the State agency may give the allotment to the center as the person's authorized representative for less than a month.
GIVEN `s 2012(m)(5) the program is a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5)(E)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual resides in the center for the purpose of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period, in months, for which the allotment is provided to the center` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(e)(1)(A) the State agency may provide an allotment for the individual to the center as an authorized representative` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(m)(5) the program is a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5)(E)` AND `the individual resides in the center for the purpose of the program` AND `the period, in months, for which the allotment is provided to the center` LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a period that is less than 1 month"
            NOTHING

-- src:1278 | (e) Allotments for households residing in centers
-- src:1279 | (1) In general
-- src:1280 | In the case of an individual who resides in a center for the purpose of a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5) of this title, a State agency may provide an allotment for the individual to—
-- src:1281 | (A) the center as an authorized representative of the individual for a period that is less than 1 month; and
-- src:1282 | (B) the individual, if the individual leaves the center.
@ref s 2017(e)(1)(B) the State agency may provide the allotment to the individual if the individual leaves the center (src:1278-1282)
GIVEN `s 2012(m)(5) the program is a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5)(E)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual resided in the center for the purpose of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has left the center` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(e)(1)(B) the State agency may provide an allotment for the individual to the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(m)(5) the program is a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5)(E)` AND `the individual resided in the center for the purpose of the program` AND `the individual has left the center` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the individual leaves the center"
            NOTHING

-- src:1283 | (2) Direct payment
-- src:1284 | A State agency may require an individual referred to in paragraph (1) to designate the center in which the individual resides as the authorized representative of the individual for the purpose of receiving an allotment.
@ref s 2017(e)(2) the State agency may require the individual to designate the center as authorized representative (src:1283-1284)
GIVEN `s 2012(m)(5) the program is a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5)(E)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual resides in the center for the purpose of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(e)(2) the State agency may require the individual to designate the center as authorized representative` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(m)(5) the program is a drug or alcoholic treatment program described in section 2012(m)(5)(E)` AND `the individual resides in the center for the purpose of the program` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an individual referred to in paragraph (1)"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2017(f) alternative procedures for residents of certain group facilities`

-- src:1286 | (1) In general
-- src:1287 | (A) Applicability
-- src:1288 | (i) In general
-- src:1289 | Subject to clause (ii), at the option of the State agency, allotments for residents of any facility described in subparagraph (B), (C), (D), or (E) of section 2012(m)(5) of this title (referred to in this subsection as a “covered facility”) may be determined and issued under this paragraph in lieu of subsection (a).
-- src:1290 | (ii) Limitation
-- src:1291 | Unless the Secretary authorizes implementation of this paragraph in all States under paragraph (3), clause (i) shall apply only to residents of covered facilities participating in a pilot project under paragraph (2).
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(A) allotments for residents of a covered facility may be determined and issued under paragraph (1) in lieu of subsection (a) (src:1286-1291)
-- In plain words: at the State agency's option, residents of a covered facility (the facilities described in section 2012(m)(5)(B) to (E)) may have their allotments worked out and issued under paragraph (1)
-- instead of subsection (a); until the Secretary authorizes this in all States, only residents of facilities in a pilot project may be treated this way.
GIVEN `s 2012(m)(5) the facility is one described in subparagraph (B), (C), (D) or (E) of section 2012(m)(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has chosen to use this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has authorized implementation of paragraph (1) in all States under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the covered facility participates in a pilot project under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(A) allotments for residents may be determined and issued under paragraph (1) in lieu of subsection (a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 2012(m)(5) the facility is one described in subparagraph (B), (C), (D) or (E) of section 2012(m)(5)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "residents of any facility described in subparagraph (B), (C), (D), or (E) of section 2012(m)(5)"
            NOTHING
        IF (NOT `the Secretary has authorized implementation of paragraph (1) in all States under paragraph (3)`) AND (NOT `the covered facility participates in a pilot project under paragraph (2)`) THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "clause (i) shall apply only to residents of covered facilities participating in a pilot project under paragraph (2)"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the State agency has chosen to use this paragraph` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the option of the State agency"
            NOTHING

-- src:1292 | (B) Amount of allotment
-- src:1293 | The allotment for each eligible resident described in subparagraph (A) shall be calculated in accordance with standardized procedures established by the Secretary that take into account the allotments typically received by residents of covered facilities.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(B) the allotment for each eligible resident (src:1292-1293)
-- In plain words: the amount comes from the Secretary's standardized procedures, which the text does not set out: it is an input, and NOTHING if none is supplied.
GIVEN `the resident is an eligible resident described in subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount calculated under the standardized procedures established by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2017(f)(1)(B) the allotment for the eligible resident` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resident is an eligible resident described in subparagraph (A)` THEN `the amount calculated under the standardized procedures established by the Secretary`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The allotment for each eligible resident described in subparagraph (A)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1294 | (C) Issuance of allotment
-- src:1295 | (i) In general
-- src:1296 | The State agency shall issue an allotment determined under this paragraph to a covered facility as the authorized representative of the residents of the covered facility.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(C)(i) the State agency shall issue the allotment to the covered facility as the residents' authorized representative (src:1294-1296)
GIVEN `the allotment is determined under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(C)(i) the State agency must issue the allotment to the covered facility as the authorized representative of the residents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the allotment is determined under paragraph (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an allotment determined under this paragraph"
            NOTHING

-- src:1297 | (ii) Adjustment
-- src:1298 | The Secretary shall establish procedures to ensure that a covered facility does not receive a greater proportion of a resident’s monthly allotment than the proportion of the month during which the resident lived in the covered facility.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(C)(ii) a covered facility does not receive a greater proportion of a resident's monthly allotment than the proportion of the month the resident lived there (src:1297-1298)
GIVEN `the monthly allotment of the resident` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of the month the resident lived in the covered facility` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2017(f)(1)(C)(ii) the greatest part of the resident's monthly allotment the covered facility may receive` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of days in the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the number of days of the month the resident lived in the covered facility` LESS THAN 0 OR `the number of days of the month the resident lived in the covered facility` GREATER THAN `the number of days in the month` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the monthly allotment of the resident` TIMES `the number of days of the month the resident lived in the covered facility` DIVIDED BY `the number of days in the month`)

-- src:1299 | (D) Departures of residents of covered facilities
-- src:1300 | (i) Notification
-- src:1301 | Any covered facility that receives an allotment for a resident under this paragraph shall—
-- src:1302 | (I) notify the State agency promptly on the departure of the resident; and
-- src:1303 | (II) notify the resident, before the departure of the resident, that the resident—
-- src:1304 | (aa) is eligible for continued benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1305 | (bb) should contact the State agency concerning continuation of the benefits.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(D)(i) what a covered facility must tell a departing resident (src:1299-1305)
-- In plain words: before a resident leaves, the facility must tell the resident that they are still eligible for SNAP benefits and should contact the State agency about continuing them.
-- (The facility must also tell the State agency promptly on the departure: that is the next function.)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 2017(f)(1)(D)(i)(II) what the covered facility must tell the resident before the departure` MEANS
    LIST "the resident is eligible for continued benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
       , "the resident should contact the State agency concerning continuation of the benefits"

-- src:1299 | (D) Departures of residents of covered facilities
-- src:1300 | (i) Notification
-- src:1301 | Any covered facility that receives an allotment for a resident under this paragraph shall—
-- src:1302 | (I) notify the State agency promptly on the departure of the resident; and
-- src:1303 | (II) notify the resident, before the departure of the resident, that the resident—
-- src:1304 | (aa) is eligible for continued benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1305 | (bb) should contact the State agency concerning continuation of the benefits.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(D)(i) the covered facility has given the required notifications (src:1299-1305)
GIVEN `the covered facility receives an allotment for the resident under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the covered facility notified the State agency promptly on the departure of the resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the covered facility notified the resident, before the departure, of both things required by subclause (II)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(D)(i) the covered facility has given the notifications` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the covered facility receives an allotment for the resident under this paragraph` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any covered facility that receives an allotment for a resident under this paragraph"
            NOTHING
        IF `the covered facility notified the State agency promptly on the departure of the resident` AND `the covered facility notified the resident, before the departure, of both things required by subclause (II)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall— (I) notify the State agency promptly on the departure of the resident"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1306 | (ii) Issuance to departed residents
-- src:1307 | On receiving a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident, the State agency—
-- src:1308 | (I) shall promptly issue the departed resident an allotment for the days of the month after the departure of the resident (calculated in a manner prescribed by the Secretary) unless the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1309 | (II) may issue an allotment for the month following the month of the departure (but not any subsequent month) based on this paragraph unless the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
-- src:1310 | (iii) State option
-- src:1311 | The State agency may elect not to issue an allotment under clause (ii)(I) if the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(D)(ii)(I) the State agency shall promptly issue the departed resident an allotment for the days after the departure (src:1306-1311)
-- In plain words: when the facility tells the State agency a resident has left, the State agency must promptly issue the departed resident an allotment for the rest of that month,
-- unless the resident reapplies, or the State agency lacks enough information on where the resident is and elects under clause (iii) not to.
GIVEN `the State agency has received a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the departed resident has reapplied to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has elected not to issue the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(D)(ii)(I) the State agency must issue the departed resident an allotment for the days of the month after the departure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency has received a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On receiving a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident"
            NOTHING
        IF `the departed resident has reapplied to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the State agency has elected not to issue the allotment` AND `s 2017(f)(1)(D)(iii) the State agency may elect not to issue an allotment under clause (ii)(I)` `the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The State agency may elect not to issue an allotment under clause (ii)(I)"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1306 | (ii) Issuance to departed residents
-- src:1307 | On receiving a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident, the State agency—
-- src:1308 | (I) shall promptly issue the departed resident an allotment for the days of the month after the departure of the resident (calculated in a manner prescribed by the Secretary) unless the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1309 | (II) may issue an allotment for the month following the month of the departure (but not any subsequent month) based on this paragraph unless the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(D)(ii)(II) the State agency may issue an allotment for the month following the month of the departure, but not any subsequent month (src:1306-1309)
GIVEN `the State agency has received a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the departed resident has reapplied to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months after the month of the departure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(D)(ii)(II) the State agency may issue an allotment for the month based on this paragraph` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency has received a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On receiving a notification under clause (i)(I) concerning the departure of a resident"
            NOTHING
        IF `the departed resident has reapplied to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of months after the month of the departure` GREATER THAN 1 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(but not any subsequent month)"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of months after the month of the departure` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the month following the month of the departure"
            NOTHING

-- src:1310 | (iii) State option
-- src:1311 | The State agency may elect not to issue an allotment under clause (ii)(I) if the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(D)(iii) the State agency may elect not to issue an allotment under clause (ii)(I) (src:1310-1311)
GIVEN `the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(D)(iii) the State agency may elect not to issue an allotment under clause (ii)(I)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the State agency lacks sufficient information on the location of the departed resident to provide the allotment"
            NOTHING

-- src:1312 | (iv) Effect of reapplication
-- src:1313 | If the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, the allotment of the departed resident shall be determined without regard to this paragraph.
@ref s 2017(f)(1)(D)(iv) effect of reapplication (src:1312-1313)
GIVEN `the departed resident has reapplied to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(1)(D)(iv) the allotment of the departed resident is determined without regard to paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the departed resident has reapplied to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the departed resident reapplies to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            NOTHING

-- src:1314 | (2) Pilot projects
-- src:1315 | (A) In general
-- src:1316 | Before the Secretary authorizes implementation of paragraph (1) in all States, the Secretary shall carry out, at the request of 1 or more State agencies and in 1 or more areas of the United States, such number of pilot projects as the Secretary determines to be sufficient to test the feasibility of determining and issuing allotments to residents of covered facilities under paragraph (1) in lieu of subsection (a).
@ref s 2017(f)(2)(A) the Secretary shall carry out pilot projects before authorizing implementation in all States (src:1314-1316)
-- In plain words: before authorizing paragraph (1) in all States, the Secretary must carry out, at the request of one or more State agencies, as many pilot projects as the Secretary judges sufficient.
-- Done means the Secretary has carried them out; the text gives no date, so not yet done is NOTHING, never a breach.
GIVEN `one or more State agencies have requested pilot projects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has authorized implementation of paragraph (1) in all States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has carried out the pilot projects the Secretary determined to be sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(2)(A) the Secretary has carried out the pilot projects required before authorizing implementation in all States` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has carried out the pilot projects the Secretary determined to be sufficient` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the pilot projects must be carried out
            NOTHING

-- src:1317 | (B) Project plan
-- src:1318 | To be eligible to participate in a pilot project under subparagraph (A), a State agency shall submit to the Secretary for approval a project plan that includes—
-- src:1319 | (i) a specification of the covered facilities in the State that will participate in the pilot project;
-- src:1320 | (ii) a schedule for reports to be submitted to the Secretary on the pilot project;
-- src:1321 | (iii) procedures for standardizing allotment amounts that takes into account the allotments typically received by residents of covered facilities; and
-- src:1322 | (iv) a commitment to carry out the pilot project in compliance with the requirements of this subsection other than paragraph (1)(B).
@ref s 2017(f)(2)(B) the project plan of a State agency meets the content requirement (src:1317-1322)
-- In plain words: to take part in a pilot project a State agency must submit a plan that includes (i) the covered facilities that will take part, (ii) a reporting schedule,
-- (iii) procedures for standardizing allotment amounts, and (iv) a commitment to follow this subsection other than paragraph (1)(B).
GIVEN `the plan specifies the covered facilities in the State that will participate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes a schedule for reports to be submitted to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes procedures for standardizing allotment amounts that take into account the allotments typically received by residents of covered facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes a commitment to carry out the pilot project in compliance with this subsection other than paragraph (1)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(2)(B) the project plan includes what a State agency must submit to be eligible to participate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the plan specifies the covered facilities in the State that will participate` AND `the plan includes a schedule for reports to be submitted to the Secretary` AND `the plan includes procedures for standardizing allotment amounts that take into account the allotments typically received by residents of covered facilities` AND `the plan includes a commitment to carry out the pilot project in compliance with this subsection other than paragraph (1)(B)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible to participate in a pilot project under subparagraph (A), a State agency shall submit to the Secretary for approval a project plan that includes"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1323 | (3) Authorization of implementation in all States
-- src:1324 | (A) In general
-- src:1325 | The Secretary shall—
-- src:1326 | (i) determine whether to authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States; and
-- src:1327 | (ii) notify the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate of the determination.
@ref s 2017(f)(3)(A) the Secretary shall determine whether to authorize implementation in all States and notify the Committees (src:1323-1327)
-- In plain words: the Secretary must decide whether to authorize paragraph (1) in all States, and tell the agriculture committees of both houses. No date is stated.
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined whether to authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has notified the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate of the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(3)(A) the Secretary has determined and notified` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has determined whether to authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States` AND `the Secretary has notified the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate of the determination` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the Secretary must determine and notify
            NOTHING

-- src:1328 | (B) Determination not to authorize implementation in all States
-- src:1329 | (i) In general
-- src:1330 | If the Secretary makes a finding described in clause (ii), the Secretary—
-- src:1331 | (I) shall not authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States; and
-- src:1332 | (II) shall terminate all pilot projects under paragraph (2) within a reasonable period of time (as determined by the Secretary).
-- src:1333 | (ii) Finding
-- src:1334 | The finding referred to in clause (i) is that—
-- src:1335 | (I) an insufficient number of project plans that the Secretary determines to be eligible for approval are submitted by State agencies under paragraph (2)(B); or
-- src:1336 | (II)
-- src:1337 | (aa) a sufficient number of pilot projects have been carried out under paragraph (2)(A); and
-- src:1338 | (bb) authorization of implementation of paragraph (1) in all States is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2017(f)(3)(B)(ii) the finding that stops authorization in all States (src:1328-1338)
-- In plain words: the finding is either (I) too few eligible project plans were submitted, or (II) enough pilot projects were carried out AND all-State authorization is not in the program's best interest.
GIVEN `an insufficient number of project plans that the Secretary determines to be eligible for approval are submitted by State agencies under paragraph (2)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sufficient number of pilot projects have been carried out under paragraph (2)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorization of implementation of paragraph (1) in all States is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(3)(B)(ii) the finding exists` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an insufficient number of project plans that the Secretary determines to be eligible for approval are submitted by State agencies under paragraph (2)(B)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a sufficient number of pilot projects have been carried out under paragraph (2)(A)` AND `authorization of implementation of paragraph (1) in all States is not in the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The finding referred to in clause (i) is that"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1328 | (B) Determination not to authorize implementation in all States
-- src:1329 | (i) In general
-- src:1330 | If the Secretary makes a finding described in clause (ii), the Secretary—
-- src:1331 | (I) shall not authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States; and
-- src:1332 | (II) shall terminate all pilot projects under paragraph (2) within a reasonable period of time (as determined by the Secretary).
@ref s 2017(f)(3)(B)(i)(I) if the finding is made the Secretary shall not authorize implementation in all States (src:1328-1332)
GIVEN `the finding described in clause (ii) exists` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(3)(B)(i)(I) the Secretary may authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the finding described in clause (ii) exists` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Secretary makes a finding described in clause (ii)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1328 | (B) Determination not to authorize implementation in all States
-- src:1329 | (i) In general
-- src:1330 | If the Secretary makes a finding described in clause (ii), the Secretary—
-- src:1331 | (I) shall not authorize implementation of paragraph (1) in all States; and
-- src:1332 | (II) shall terminate all pilot projects under paragraph (2) within a reasonable period of time (as determined by the Secretary).
@ref s 2017(f)(3)(B)(i)(II) if the finding is made the Secretary shall terminate all pilot projects within a reasonable period (src:1328-1332)
GIVEN `the finding described in clause (ii) exists` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2017(f)(3)(B)(i)(II) the Secretary must terminate all pilot projects under paragraph (2) within a reasonable period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the finding described in clause (ii) exists` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Secretary makes a finding described in clause (ii)"
            NOTHING
